#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:1
msgid "Hex Worlds and a Mini-Catan Board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:3
msgid ""
"A `HexWorld` consists of hexagonal tiles. Hexes are addressed with "
"`(column, row)` coordinates, like tiles in a `TiledWorld`. Odd rows are "
"shifted half a hex to the right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:7
msgid "Actors can be placed on three kinds of positions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:9
msgid "**Tiles** (the hexes themselves), e.g. `(2, 3)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:10
msgid ""
"**Corners** (shared by up to three hexes), e.g. the `\"no\"` corner of a "
"hex"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:11
msgid "**Edges** (shared by two hexes), e.g. the `\"o\"` edge of a hex"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:13
msgid ""
"This is exactly the structure of a Catan board: land hexes, settlements "
"on corners, and roads on edges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:16
msgid "Create a hex world"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:26
msgid "Build a Catan-like board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:28
msgid ""
"The 19 land hexes of a Catan board are arranged in rows of 3, 4, 5, 4, "
"and 3 hexes. Actors placed on hexes are drawn as hexagons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:61
msgid "Click hexes, corners, and edges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:63
msgid ""
"`world.get_tile_from_pixel(mouse_pos)` returns the hex under the mouse, "
"`world.get_corner_from_pixel(mouse_pos)` the nearest corner, and "
"`world.get_edge_from_pixel(mouse_pos)` the nearest edge. All three "
"queries return `None` if the pixel is outside the world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:68
msgid ""
"The example places a settlement (small circle) on the clicked corner and "
"a road (small rectangle) on the clicked edge:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:94
msgid "Query the neighborhood"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:96
msgid ""
"`world.get_tiles_in_radius(position, radius)` returns all hexes within a "
"given hex distance. `tile.get_neighbour_tiles()` returns the up to six "
"neighbors of a hex. This is useful for Catan rules such as \"the robber "
"blocks all hexes around the desert\"."
msgstr ""

